id: smoked
name: Smoked
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock, so the Square stays Obscured until the last thrower's clock runs out
# rather than the first. The cap only has to be out of anybody's reach, as Ignited's does.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry gives Squares a Quality and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# The Environmental Quality this mark puts on the Square while it is held. Named here and
# not in the code, where no Quality is named.
quality: obscured
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Thick smoke all around you. Your Square is Obscured.
text: >
  Smoked: the Smoke Bomb's mark. "In this AoE, all Squares gain the Obscured Environmental
  Quality until the end of your next turn."

---

# Ignited's shape, for smoke: there are no Squares, so the Quality lands on the characters
# in the cloud, as a mark on the thrower's clock, and `qualitiesOf` adds the Quality in the
# `quality:` header while it is held. The player's own ticks are never written to.
#
# No effects of its own. What smoke does is the Obscured Quality's file.
